WEBVTT

00:00.259 --> 00:10.193
monday, your calendar, Slack and email in one place. About 7 hours saved a week, by our estimate.

00:10.389 --> 00:16.843
Today: your night on a timeline, with meetings, your break, and where tasks fit.

00:17.023 --> 00:21.124
Up next tells you exactly what to work on now, and what to check first.

00:21.305 --> 00:26.265
Due soon or late is your safety net: anything due in two days, or already overdue.

00:26.456 --> 00:32.083
Waiting on you counts replies, blocked work and what’s due this week. Each tile opens its page.

00:32.272 --> 00:37.109
Your schedule shows the week’s meetings, with a checklist of what to bring an hour before.

00:37.288 --> 00:40.421
And the briefing gives you a short summary with your top three.

00:41.542 --> 00:46.894
Every page also has a World view. Here, your night becomes an office you can explore.

00:47.570 --> 00:52.765
Tasks shows all your monday work, grouped by when it’s due, so urgent work sits on top.

00:52.955 --> 00:57.441
Pick one, and this panel holds your notes, a checklist, and the guides that match it.

00:58.565 --> 01:03.240
In World, tasks become crates. Late ones glow, and old ones gather dust.

01:03.919 --> 01:07.742
Clients puts the ones that need you first, then the ones you’re waiting on.

01:08.221 --> 01:11.832
Open one to see its open work and everything done lately.

01:12.020 --> 01:16.830
And notes only you can see: contacts, the website, and anything worth remembering.

01:17.959 --> 01:22.357
In World, each client is a building, and the ones that need you stand in front.

01:23.053 --> 01:28.801
Each teammate’s role, how they like to work, and what’s open between you.

01:28.987 --> 01:31.618
And this chart shows who’s awake during your shift.

01:32.739 --> 01:37.254
In World, columns are time zones, and lit rooms show who’s working right now.

01:37.936 --> 01:42.059
Replies collects every Slack message and email draft waiting on you.

01:42.236 --> 01:47.221
Open one, and a suggested reply is ready to edit. You always send it yourself.

01:47.404 --> 01:51.595
On the right, who it’s from, and anything you’ve noted about how they like to work.

01:52.836 --> 01:55.867
In World, it’s a post office where people wait in line.

01:56.551 --> 02:01.519
Projects lists every project and automation, with the ones that need a look on top.

02:01.701 --> 02:06.035
Each one shows its health, its latest problems, and the plan for what’s next.

02:06.219 --> 02:09.454
And next steps: your own short plan for each project.

02:10.687 --> 02:13.710
In World, each project is a machine in a factory.

02:14.384 --> 02:18.724
Month lays out each night: its meetings, its tasks, and how full it is.

02:18.900 --> 02:22.608
Tasks without a night wait here. Drag one onto a lighter night.

02:23.738 --> 02:27.971
In World, each night is a house, and crates on the roof mean too much work.

02:28.650 --> 02:33.065
Notes keeps your notes, to-dos, meeting notes and site issues in one place.

02:33.252 --> 02:36.644
Meeting notes arrive with your next steps already pulled out.

02:36.834 --> 02:40.939
Recent Drive docs sit right beside them, matched to your work by name.

02:42.052 --> 02:46.308
In World, it’s a library. Notes are books, and to-dos are sticky notes.

02:46.982 --> 02:53.225
Your end-of-shift report, drafted from what you finished. One click saves it and copies it for Slack.

02:53.417 --> 02:56.809
And here’s everything that went into it, so nothing gets missed.

02:57.935 --> 03:02.507
In World, each night is a lantern that lights up once its report is saved.

03:03.182 --> 03:06.716
News collects Claude and industry updates, picked for your work.

03:06.900 --> 03:10.173
Each one says why it matters to you, with steps to try it.

03:10.351 --> 03:14.555
Save anything to your try list. Time spent learning counts toward your growth.

03:15.783 --> 03:19.507
In World, it’s a street with a billboard, a cinema and a tool shed.

03:20.152 --> 03:24.218
Finally, Growth turns finished work into experience points and levels.

03:24.398 --> 03:29.327
Your skills grow with the work you actually do. A small game that never gets in the way.

03:29.515 --> 03:34.558
Certifications and your learning log count too, so learning shows up next to delivery.

03:34.709 --> 03:40.743
One place to run your shift, built on the tools you already use. Tasks are still finished in monday.
